    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Set the background canvas of a video segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type; must match this typed shortcut\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --type TEXT         Canvas type: color / blur / image\r\n          --color TEXT        Canvas color, e.g. #RRGGBBAA\r\n          --blur TEXT         Blur amount, e.g. 0.75. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --image TEXT        Local image path; exactly one image source is required for --type\r\n                              image\r\n          --image-id TEXT     Image resource id; exactly one image source is required for\r\n                              --type image\r\n          --image-name TEXT   Image name\r\n          --resource TEXT     Canvas image resource: vimo://<id> / local://<path>; exactly one\r\n                              image source is required for --type image\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: background only applies to video segments (segment_video).\r\nNOTE: --type image requires exactly one of --resource, --image-id, or --image.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Use a blurred version of the segment as the background canvas\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type blur --blur 0.75\r\n  # Use a solid color background\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type color --color #000000FF\r\n  # Use a local image as the background canvas\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type image --image /tmp/bg.jpg\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Set the background canvas of a video segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type; must match this typed shortcut\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --type TEXT         Canvas type: color / blur / image\r\n          --color TEXT        Canvas color, e.g. #RRGGBBAA\r\n          --blur TEXT         Blur amount, e.g. 0.75. Unitless scalar.\r\n          --image TEXT        Local image path; exactly one image source is required for --type\r\n                              image\r\n          --image-id TEXT     Image resource id; exactly one image source is required for\r\n                              --type image\r\n          --image-name TEXT   Image name\r\n          --resource TEXT     Canvas image resource: vimo://<id> / local://<path>; exactly one\r\n                              image source is required for --type image\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: background only applies to video segments (segment_video).\r\nNOTE: --type image requires exactly one of --resource, --image-id, or --image.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Use a blurred version of the segment as the background canvas\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type blur --blur 0.75\r\n  # Use a solid color background\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type color --color #000000FF\r\n  # Use a local image as the background canvas\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video background --seg-id <UUID> --type image --image /tmp/bg.jpg\r\n",
